WEBVTT

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.976
But that one word made
a really big difference.

00:08:02.547 --> 00:08:04.178
He then surveyed the students,

00:08:04.202 --> 00:08:06.868
and the good news was the students,
both men and women,

00:08:06.892 --> 00:08:09.286
thought Heidi and Howard
were equally competent,

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:10.588
and that's good.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.683
The bad news was
that everyone liked Howard.

00:08:13.707 --> 00:08:15.707
He's a great guy.
You want to work for him.

00:08:15.731 --> 00:08:17.731
You want to spend the day
fishing with him.

00:08:17.755 --> 00:08:19.317
But Heidi? Not so sure.

00:08:19.341 --> 00:08:22.206
She's a little out for herself.
She's a little political.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.277
You're not sure
you'd want to work for her.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.625
This is the complication.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.310
We have to tell our daughters
and our colleagues,

00:08:29.334 --> 00:08:32.018
we have to tell ourselves
to believe we got the A,